WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.330
All right, we're starting the week off with
something a little wacky, something I wish

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.220
we weren't actually having to start the week
off.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:14.491
The New York Times editorial board has written
an article called Ease Up on the Executive

00:00:14.491 --> 00:00:15.491
Actions.

00:00:15.491 --> 00:00:21.580
Joe with the subtitle, President Biden is
right to not let his agenda be held hostage,

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:27.140
but legislating through Congress is a better
path.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:33.539
And in this article, The New York Times editorial
board says correctly that, quote, A week into

00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:39.239
his presidency, Mr Biden has issued a raft
of executive orders and other actions already.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:44.309
He is committed to rejoining the Paris climate
change agreement ended the Muslim travel ban,

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:50.839
canceled the permit for the Keystone XL pipeline,
rescinded funding for and halted construction

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:57.089
on the wall at the southern border, reaffirmed
the Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals

00:00:57.089 --> 00:01:05.420
program mandated wearing a mask, wearing on
federal grounds, moved to end the federal

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:11.740
government's reliance on private prisons,
reversed the ban on transgender military service,

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:18.280
and called for agency assessments aimed at
advancing racial equity, just to name a few.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.240
The coming days will bring more such action.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.500
But this isn't that good, they say.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.630
And they're concerned.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:30.490
They say, not just because executive orders
don't create law and can be changed by future

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:37.259
by future presidents, which is true, but because,
quote, executive actions are far more ephemeral

00:01:37.259 --> 00:01:42.799
and easily discarded than legislation which
can set up a whipsaw effect as each president

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:47.289
scrambles to undo the work of his predecessor,
just as Mr. Trump said about reversing as

00:01:47.289 --> 00:01:52.049
many of President Barack Obama's directives
as possible, Mr. Biden is now working to reverse

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:55.320
many of Mr. Trump's reversals with executive
orders.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.020
There is always another presidential election
just a few years off, threatening to upend

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.219
everything.

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:04.979
This is one of the silliest New York Times
editorials I've seen.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:11.090
First of all, these executive orders are a
good start until permanent legislation can

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.300
be passed, if it can.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:18.570
And the if right now is arguably more important
than it's ever been, given that there is a

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:22.520
Republican Party that doesn't even pretend
to care about policy.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.871
What it Marjorie Taylor Green run on, other
than just Trump ism and owning the Libs, what

00:02:26.871 --> 00:02:31.040
did Lauren Bobert run on other than Trump
ism and owning the Libs?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.090
This is one of the two year period during
which Democrats have control of the House,

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.870
Senate and White House, and they may have
no choice but to go at everything by themselves.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.910
So we'll talk more about that.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:49.530
Secondly, these executive orders are a signal
that hopefully Joe Biden is going to do everything

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:55.510
he can of the things he promised to do, regardless
of whether he has Republican support or not.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:59.140
And remember, he was elected based on the
things he promised to do.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:03.560
And number three, this reeks of status quo
ism from The New York Times.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:08.750
The New York Times editorial board doesn't
like that Joe Biden isn't using the powers

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:14.040
he has after being elected by voters because
it's too much change.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:21.190
What and fourth, much of what Joe Biden is
doing isn't really a dramatic change anyway

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:24.220
beyond getting us back to the pre Trump situation.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:05:14.520
So in a way, like I hate to say it, but Joe
Biden's executive orders are, in 

00:05:14.520 --> 00:06:25.300
a sense, getting 

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:50.930
us 

00:06:50.930 --> 00:07:01.639
back 

00:07:01.639 --> 00:07:15.500
to the 

00:07:15.500 --> 00:08:24.710
status quo.

